      "claim": "Amoxicillin, which shares the same 4-hydroxyphenylglycyl alpha-aminoacyl side chain as the query, has absolute oral bioavailability of about 77-93% in healthy humans across 250-1000 mg doses, and lower but still above-threshold estimates of about 55-59% in frail elderly and paediatric patients.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive",
      "molecule_ids": ["Molecule 3", "Molecule 4"],
      "record_ids": ["Record 3-1", "Record 3-2", "Record 3-3", "Record 4-1", "Record 4-2", "Record 4-3", "Record 4-4", "Record 4-5", "Record 4-6", "Record 4-7", "Record 4-8", "Record 4-9", "Record 4-10"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Cefroxadine, a close oral aminocephalosporin, showed nearly 100% oral bioavailability in humans, and a structurally similar cephalosporin with a 4-hydroxyphenylglycyl side chain showed about 40% oral bioavailability, both supporting the pass prediction.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive",
      "molecule_ids": ["Molecule 5", "Molecule 8"],
      "record_ids": ["Record 5-1", "Record 8-1"]
